{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1385731-dual-paradigm","id":1385731,"title":"Dual Paradigm?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-05-04T21:04:01-07:00","id":1385731,"title":"Dual Paradigm?","content":"I know that the systems have changed, but did the dual paradigm merit survive in some form in M20?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-04T21:22:58-07:00","id":1385735,"title":"","content":"I remember talking about this when M20 dropped, but I don't think its a thing anymore because they made forming your Paradigm more flexible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-04T21:28:23-07:00","id":1385736,"title":"","content":"There's a Dual Affiliation Merit (Book of Secrets pp.79\u201380) that represents having been initiated and trained in two different Awakened groups. You're paying for the ability to have two Affinity Spheres, one from each group. You don't get \u201ctwo different paradigms\u201d because M20 goes with the notion that every mage has one Focus; and if he can't synthesize the competing beliefs from his various teachers into a single, cohesive whole, he doesn't have a valid Focus. That said, a former Verbena who changes affiliation to the Order of Hermes can synthesize both Witchcraft and High Ritual Magic into her Focus, effectively synthesizing a hybrid of Verbena-style and Hermetic-style magic as her personal Focus; no need to spend points to do it, as anyone can do it for free. <br /> <br /> If one of the groups that trained you was technomantic and the other was mystical, then you also want the Scientific Mystic or Techgnosi Merit (pp.45\u201346), depending on whether you approach mysticism from a scientific mindset or vice versa; but that's an update of the Scientific Mystic Merit from the Revised Sons of Ether Tradition Book, not the Dual Paradigm Merit from Initiates of the Art. The latter became the Dual Affiliation Merit I mentioned earlier.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 05-05-2020, 02:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","r